Switch runtime hooks in the platform layer (__SWITCH__).

- threads that run game code switch onto their low stacks themselves
  (PORT_LOW_STACK_CALL, as on 64-bit Windows; sms-switch stack_switch.cpp),
  since libnx maps every thread stack again above 4 GiB
- sleep with nanosleep (newlib has no clock_nanosleep), time zone offset from
  the console (no tm_gmtoff), no signal crash handler (Horizon has no
  signals), memory probing through sms_switch_read_memory
- MEM1 from sms_switch_mem1_window: at 0x80000000 unless the loader is there,
  else another window below 4 GiB, with the SDK's address translations, J3D
  texture commands, boot info and the renderer following it (decomp-patches
  switch-01/02, the Android branch's android-02/03 for the Switch)

diff --git a/decomp-patches/switch-01-mem1-addresses.patch b/decomp-patches/switch-01-mem1-addresses.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0eb3e54
--- /dev/null
+++ b/decomp-patches/switch-01-mem1-addresses.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+Reason: Android and Switch MEM1 relocation must keep SDK physical/cached aliases consistent with the arena and renderer, without truncating high heap pointers.
+--- a/libs/dolphin/include/dolphin/os.h
++++ b/libs/dolphin/include/dolphin/os.h
+@@ -174 +174,12 @@
+-#if !DEBUG
++#if defined(TARGET_PC) && (defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(__SWITCH__))
++// Android or the Switch may occupy the GameCube addresses. The port reserves
++// another arena that fits raw u32 pointer slots; CPU cached/uncached aliases
++// share that mapping, and physical addresses are relative to its base.
++extern u8* port_mem1_base;
++#define OSPhysicalToCached(paddr) ((void*)((u64)port_mem1_base + (u32)(paddr)))
++#define OSPhysicalToUncached(paddr) OSPhysicalToCached(paddr)
++#define OSCachedToPhysical(caddr) ((u32)((u64)(caddr) - (u64)port_mem1_base))
++#define OSUncachedToPhysical(ucaddr) OSCachedToPhysical(ucaddr)
++#define OSCachedToUncached(caddr) ((void*)(caddr))
++#define OSUncachedToCached(ucaddr) ((void*)(ucaddr))
++#elif !DEBUG
